<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carol II of Romania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893–1953</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carol II was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> from 1930 to 1940. Having renounced his rights to the throne in 1925, he returned in 1930 to displace his young son Michael, and in 1938 he abolished the political parties and set up a royal dictatorship. After Romania lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukovina">Bukovina</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-dobruja">Southern Dobruja</a> in 1940, he was forced to abdicate in favour of Michael and went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carol-ii-of-romania.jpg" alt="Carol II of Romania" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carol_II_of_Romania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
